    "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n    <title>Agentic Coding Research Report - 2026-05-12</title>\n    <style>\n        /* Reset and Base Styles */\n        * {\n            margin: 0;\n            padding: 0;\n            box-sizing: border-box;\n        }\n\n        body {\n            font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 13px;\n            line-height: 1.5;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        a {\n            color: #000000;\n            text-decoration: none;\n        }\n\n        a:hover {\n            text-decoration: underline;\n        }\n\n        /* Container */\n        .container {\n            max-width: 1400px;\n            margin: 0 auto;\n            padding: 0 10px;\n        }\n\n        /* Header */\n        header {\n            background-color: #ff6600;\n            padding: 10px 0;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        header .container {\n            display: flex;\n            justify-content: space-between;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .logo {\n            font-weight: bold;\n            font-size: 16px;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .date {\n            color: #000000;\n            font-size: 12px;\n        }\n\n        /* Navigation */\n        nav {\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            padding: 10px 0;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        nav .container {\n            display: flex;\n            gap: 20px;\n        }\n\n        nav a {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 12px;\n        }\n\n        nav a:hover {\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        /* Main Content */\n        main {\n            padding: 20px 0;\n        }\n\n        .three-column-layout {\n            display: grid;\n            grid-template-columns: 40% 35% 25%;\n            gap: 20px;\n            align-items: start;\n        }\n\n        /* Section Styles */\n        section {\n            background-color: #ffffff;\n            border: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            padding: 15px;\n        }\n\n        section h2 {\n            font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n            font-size: 14px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-bottom: 15px;\n            padding-bottom: 10px;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n        }\n\n        /* Item List Styles */\n        .item-list {\n            list-style: none;\n        }\n\n        .item {\n            padding: 10px 0;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .item:last-child {\n            border-bottom: none;\n        }\n\n        .item-title {\n            font-weight: bold;\n            margin-bottom: 5px;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a {\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .item-title a:visited {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        .item-description {\n            color: #000000;\n            margin-bottom: 8px;\n            font-size: 12px;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            display: flex;\n            flex-wrap: wrap;\n            gap: 10px;\n        }\n\n        .item-meta span {\n            display: inline-flex;\n            align-items: center;\n        }\n\n        .tag {\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n        }\n\n        .update-badge {\n            display: inline-block;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n            font-weight: bold;\n            text-transform: uppercase;\n        }\n\n        .update-badge.feature {\n            background-color: #ffe4c4;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .update-badge.bugfix {\n            background-color: #f0d0d0;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .update-badge.release {\n            background-color: #d4edda;\n            color: #000000;\n        }\n\n        .source-badge {\n            background-color: #e6f3ff;\n            padding: 2px 6px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 10px;\n        }\n\n        /* Insight specific styles */\n        .insight-item {\n            padding: 12px 0;\n            border-bottom: 1px solid #eeeeee;\n        }\n\n        .insight-meta {\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            margin-top: 8px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-points {\n            margin-top: 8px;\n            padding-left: 20px;\n        }\n\n        .insight-points li {\n            color: #000000;\n            font-size: 11px;\n            margin-bottom: 4px;\n        }\n\n        /* Empty State */\n        .empty-state {\n            text-align: center;\n            color: #828282;\n            padding: 40px 20px;\n            font-style: italic;\n        }\n\n        /* Footer */\n        footer {\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            padding: 20px 0;\n            border-top: 1px solid #d4d4d4;\n            margin-top: 30px;\n        }\n\n        footer .container {\n            text-align: center;\n            color: #828282;\n            font-size: 11px;\n        }\n\n        footer a {\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        /* Responsive Design */\n        @media (max-width: 1200px) {\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n            }\n\n            .technical-insights {\n                grid-column: 1 / -1;\n            }\n        }\n\n        @media (max-width: 768px) {\n            .three-column-layout {\n                grid-template-columns: 1fr;\n            }\n\n            header .container {\n                flex-direction: column;\n                gap: 10px;\n            }\n\n            nav .container {\n                flex-wrap: wrap;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Print Styles */\n        @media print {\n            body {\n                background-color: #ffffff;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                page-break-inside: avoid;\n            }\n\n            a {\n                color: #000000;\n                text-decoration: underline;\n            }\n\n            .three-column-layout {\n                display: block;\n            }\n\n            section {\n                margin-bottom: 20px;\n            }\n        }\n\n        /* Code and Monospace Elements */\n        code {\n            font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n            background-color: #f6f6ef;\n            padding: 2px 4px;\n            border-radius: 2px;\n            font-size: 11px;\n        }\n\n        /* External Link Indicator */\n        .external-link::after {\n            content: \" ↗\";\n            font-size: 10px;\n            color: #828282;\n        }\n\n        /* Scrollbar Styling */\n        ::-webkit-scrollbar {\n            width: 8px;\n            height: 8px;\n        }\n\n        ::-webkit-scrollbar-track {\n            background: #f6f6ef;\n        }\n\n        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb {\n            background: #d4d4d4;\n            border-radius: 4px;\n        }\n\n        ::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb:hover {\n            background: #828282;\n        }\n    </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n    <header>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <div class=\"logo\">AgentDaily</div>\n            <div class=\"date\">May 12, 2026</div>\n        </div>\n    </header>\n\n    <nav>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a>\n            <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Whitelist Updates</a>\n            <a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a>\n        </div>\n    </nav>\n\n    <main>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <div class=\"three-column-layout\">\n                <!-- New Products Section -->\n                <section class=\"new-products\" id=\"new-products\">\n                    <h2>New Products</h2>\n                    <ul class=\"item-list\">\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/ab-613/opengravity\" class=\"external-link\">OpenGravity</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                A zero-install, BYOK vanilla JS clone of Antigravity - full AI IDE with WebContainer API integration for real terminal environments. Built to avoid usage limits on closed-source AI IDEs.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span class=\"tag\">AI IDE</span>\n                                <span class=\"source-badge\">GitHub</span>\n                                <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://producthunt.com/posts/graphbit-prflow\" class=\"external-link\">Graphbit PRFlow - AI Code Review Agent</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                AI code review agent that automates PR reviews with workflow orchestration. Integrates into development workflows to catch security issues and learn team standards.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span class=\"tag\">code agent</span>\n                                <span class=\"source-badge\">Product Hunt</span>\n                                <span>2026-05-07</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                    </ul>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Whitelist Updates Section -->\n                <section class=\"whitelist-updates\" id=\"whitelist-updates\">\n                    <h2>Whitelist Updates</h2>\n                    <ul class=\"item-list\">\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Claude Code <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.139: Agent View, /goal command, transcript navigation</strong><br>\n                                Added agent view (Research Preview) showing all sessions with running/blocked/done states, /goal command to set completion conditions with live elapsed/turns/tokens tracking, /scroll-speed command, plugin details command, transcript view navigation with keyboard shortcuts, hook args and continueOnBlock options, and CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR for MCP servers. Fixed numerous bugs including deadlocks, MCP connection issues, and terminal rendering problems.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-12</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Claude Code <span class=\"update-badge release\">release</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.138: Internal fixes</strong><br>\n                                Minor version with internal stability improvements and fixes.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-08</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Claude Code <span class=\"update-badge bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.137: VSCode extension Windows fix</strong><br>\n                                Fixed VSCode extension failing to activate on Windows systems.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-07</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Claude Code <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.136: Enterprise feedback surveys, Auto Mode hard deny rules, extensive stability fixes</strong><br>\n                                Added enterprise feedback survey support via OpenTelemetry, auto mode hard deny classifier rules that unconditionally block actions, fixed MCP servers/plugins disappearing after /clear, OAuth refresh token issues for remote MCP servers, login loops, API errors with extended thinking, and over 30 additional bug fixes across Windows clipboard, WSL2 image paste, terminal rendering, and plugin systems.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-06</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Claude Code <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>Week 19: Plugins from .zip archives and URLs</strong><br>\n                                Claude Code v2.1.128–v2.1.136 introduced plugin loading from .zip archives and URLs via --plugin-url flag, worktree.baseRef setting to choose branching source, auto mode hard deny rules, and hooks now expose effort level via effort.level and $CLAUDE_EFFORT environment variable.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-04</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://code.claude.com/docs/en/whats-new\" class=\"external-link\">What's New</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Cursor <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>Bugbot Effort Levels and PR Review enhancements</strong><br>\n                                Teams admins and individual users can now customize the Bugbot's effort level for PR reviews with three configurations: Default (optimized for speed), High (more reasoning, more expensive), or Custom (natural language instructions). Also introduced new PR review experience with inline review threads, commits tab, and changes tab with file tree navigation.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\">Changelog</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Cursor <span class=\"update-badge bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v3.3: Cloud agent reliability fixes</strong><br>\n                                Fixed various cloud agent timing and hydration edge cases that could degrade reliability.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-06</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://cursor.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\">Changelog</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Windsurf <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.2.17: Devin Review, Agent Command Center, Windows fixes</strong><br>\n                                All Windsurf IDE users now have access to Devin Review and Quick Review with existing subscriptions (2 week free trial for self-serve). Added Agent Command Center with list display option, improved sessions sidebar sorting and filtering. Fixed Windows update bug preventing some users from upgrading. Fixed bugs with MCP servers and improved Devin Local agent reliability.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-06</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\">Changelog</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Windsurf <span class=\"update-badge bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.32: Bug fixes for Cascade crashes and auth</strong><br>\n                                Fixed crash when switching between Cascade conversations, authentication issue preventing Devin Cloud sessions from starting, and issue where responses to agent questions were not sent correctly.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-04-29</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\">Changelog</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Windsurf <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v2.1.29: Devin for Terminal and Local agent</strong><br>\n                                Devin is now available for Terminal with CLI agent, optimized for interactive work with full access to codebase. Seamless hand off to Devin in cloud with VM, testing, and video recordings. Multi-model support including Opus 4.7, GPT-5.5, and SWE-1.6. Devin Local agent in Windsurf is up to 30% more token-efficient than Cascade agent.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-04-28</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://windsurf.com/changelog\" class=\"external-link\">Changelog</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Aider <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v0.56.0: Prompt caching, /report command, chat language</strong><br>\n                                Enables prompt caching for Sonnet via OpenRouter and 8k output tokens for Sonnet via VertexAI and DeepSeek V2.5. New /report command opens browser with pre-populated GitHub Issue. New --chat-language switch to set spoken language. Renamed --models to --list-models. Numerous bug fixes for corner case crashes.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-08</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Aider <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v0.55.0: GitHub issue crash reports, /settings command</strong><br>\n                                Offer to submit GitHub issue pre-filled with uncaught exception info. New /settings command to show active settings. Startup improvements with git repo sanity checks and model sanity check confirmation pauses. Include important devops files in repo map. Converted many error messages to warning messages.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-01</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/paul-gauthier/aider/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Continue <span class=\"update-badge feature\">feature</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v1.3.38: Config filtering, configs support</strong><br>\n                                Filter session history by workspace directory. Add .continue/configs support. Ensure config.yaml exists and is populated when accessed. Bumped dependencies for happy-dom, handlebars, brace-expansion, and path-to-regexp.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-08</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                Continue <span class=\"update-badge bugfix\">bugfix</span>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                <strong>v1.3.36: Security fixes, JetBrains improvements, ClawRouter provider</strong><br>\n                                Resolve critical and high security vulnerabilities. Fix StringIndexOutOfBoundsException in readRangeInFile. Hardened JetBrains remote config sync to prevent IDE freezes. Fixed crashes in DiffStreamHandler, memory leaks in CoreMessenger, and chunked large JCEF messages. Added ClawRouter as provider for cost-optimized model routing.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-meta\">\n                                <span>2026-05-01</span>\n                                <span>·</span>\n                                <a href=\"https://github.com/continuedev/continue/releases\" class=\"external-link\">Release Notes</a>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                    </ul>\n                </section>\n\n                <!-- Technical Insights Section -->\n                <section class=\"technical-insights\" id=\"technical-insights\">\n                    <h2>Technical Insights</h2>\n                    <ul class=\"item-list\">\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812345\" class=\"external-link\">I'm going back to writing code by hand</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                A popular Hacker News discussion (814 points) about developers choosing to return to manual coding despite advances in AI coding tools. The article explores the trade-offs between AI-assisted coding and traditional development workflows, highlighting concerns about skill atrophy and the value of manual coding expertise.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>k10s.dev</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40811987\" class=\"external-link\">Local AI needs to be the norm</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Highly discussed Hacker News post (1669 points, 656 comments) advocating for local AI deployment. The community discussion explores privacy, cost, and control benefits of running AI models locally versus cloud-based solutions.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>unix.foo</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40812754\" class=\"external-link\">Running local models on an M4 with 24GB memory</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Practical guide and discussion (498 points) about running local LLMs on Apple's M4 hardware with 24GB RAM. The community shares experiences with model sizing, quantization, and performance optimization for local inference.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>jola.dev</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40811543\" class=\"external-link\">Software engineering may no longer be a lifetime career</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Thought-provoking discussion (166 points, 301 comments) about the sustainability of software engineering as a long-term career in the age of AI.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>seangoedecke.com</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40813210\" class=\"external-link\">Mythos Finds a Curl Vulnerability</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Claude Mythos discovered a vulnerability in curl, highlighting the growing capability of AI systems in security research. The post (520 points, 218 comments) discusses implications for automated vulnerability discovery.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>haxx.se</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=40811876\" class=\"external-link\">An AI coding agent needs to reduce maintenance costs</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                James Shore explores the economic reality of AI coding agents - they should reduce maintenance costs, not just initial development time. Discussion (316 points) about long-term code quality and maintainability.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>jamesshore.com</span> · <span>HN</span> · <span>2026-05-11</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/10/nyt-ai-hallucination-correction/\" class=\"external-link\">NYT AI Hallucination Correction</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                The New York Times issued an editors' note after learning that a remark attributed to Pierre Poilievre was actually an AI-generated summary of his views that AI rendered as a quotation.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-10</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://changelog.com/podcast/587\" class=\"external-link\">Intent, Amelia Wattenberger, and the agent-first redesign</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Amelia Wattenberger discusses designing Intent at Augment Code in an agent-first world. Key insight: 'the last 30% of any software project is about to become the hardest part you've ever done.'\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>The Changelog</span> · <span>Podcast</span> · <span>2026-05-10</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/8/using-claude-code-the-unreasonable-effectiveness-of-html/\" class=\"external-link\">The Unreasonable Effectiveness of HTML</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Thariq Shihipar advocates for HTML over Markdown as an output format for Claude. HTML enables SVG diagrams, interactive widgets, in-page navigation, and richer explanations.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-08</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/08/how-anthropics-mythos-firefox-cybersecurity/\" class=\"external-link\">How Anthropic's Mythos has rewritten Firefox's approach to cybersecurity</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                TechCrunch covers how Mozilla used Claude Mythos to dramatically scale up vulnerability discovery in Firefox, going from 20-30 bugs per month to 423 in April.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Russell Brandom</span> · <span>TechCrunch</span> · <span>2026-05-08</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/7/behind-the-scenes-hardening-firefox-with-claude-mythos-preview/\" class=\"external-link\">Hardening Firefox with Claude Mythos Preview</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Mozilla used access to Claude Mythos preview to locate and fix hundreds of vulnerabilities in Firefox. They went from fixing 20-30 security bugs per month to 423 in April 2026 alone.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-07</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://techcrunch.com/2026/05/07/cloudflare-ai-jobs-obsolete-revenue-record/\" class=\"external-link\">AI made 1,100 jobs obsolete at Cloudflare</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Cloudflare revealed that AI automation eliminated 1,100 positions while the company achieved record revenue. Raises important questions about AI's impact on employment.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Julie Bort</span> · <span>TechCrunch</span> · <span>2026-05-07</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/notes-on-the-xai-anthropic-data-center-deal/\" class=\"external-link\">Notes on the xAI/Anthropic data center deal</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Anthropic struck a deal with SpaceX/xAI to use 'all of the capacity of their Colossus data center'. This was one of the biggest announcements from Anthropic's Code w/ Claude 2026 event.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-06</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/6/vibe-coding-and-agentic-engineering/\" class=\"external-link\">Vibe coding and agentic engineering are getting closer</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Simon discusses his disturbing realization that vibe coding and agentic engineering have started to converge in his own work.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-06</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                        <li class=\"insight-item\">\n                            <div class=\"item-title\">\n                                <a href=\"https://simonwillison.net/2026/May/5/our-ai-started-a-cafe-in-stockholm/\" class=\"external-link\">Our AI started a cafe in Stockholm</a>\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"item-description\">\n                                Andon Labs ran an AI-run cafe experiment in Stockholm, Sweden. While sometimes amusing (ordering 120 eggs for a cafe with no stove), it raises ethical concerns when AI managers waste time of humans who haven't opted into the experiment.\n                            </div>\n                            <div class=\"insight-meta\">\n                                <span>Simon Willison</span> · <span>Blog</span> · <span>2026-05-05</span>\n                            </div>\n                        </li>\n                    </ul>\n                </section>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </main>\n\n    <footer>\n        <div class=\"container\">\n            <p>AgentDaily - Agentic Coding Research Report</p>\n            <p>\n                <a href=\"#\">Archive</a> ·\n                <a href=\"#\">About</a> ·\n                <a href=\"#\">RSS</a>\n            </p>\n            <p>Generated on May 12, 2026</p>\n        </div>\n    </footer>\n</body>\n</html>",
